The new static migration guard has a bypass for valid SQLite UPDATE statements with subqueries in earlier SET expressions, so it does not fully enforce the invariant it is introduced to protect.

Review comment:

- [P2] Do not truncate SET at subquery FROM — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s25/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-schema/src/lib.rs:1471-1474
  When a pinned-table `UPDATE` has an earlier assignment containing a subquery before the `logical_id` assignment, e.g. `UPDATE canonical_nodes SET body=(SELECT body FROM old), logical_id='x' ...`, this helper stops the SET clause at the subquery's `FROM` and never sees `LOGICAL_ID`. That lets `check_migration_logical_id_pin` accept a real migration backfill that populates `logical_id` on existing canonical rows.
